# Day 10/60 — Building a Personal Portfolio Website with Claude

## Objective

Learn how AI can be used to create a complete portfolio website from a structured prompt.

## Task

Generate a portfolio website using Claude, customize it with personal information, test the output, and deploy it online.

## Final Output

Live Portfolio:

https://projectnexus1.netlify.app/

## Process

1. Open Claude
2. Use the provided Portfolio Website prompt
3. Replace placeholders with personal details
4. Generate website code
5. Save the HTML file
6. Test functionality
7. Deploy online

## What I Learned

### AI Can Build Complete Web Experiences

Claude was able to generate:

* Portfolio structure
* Project sections
* Responsive layouts
* Professional design elements
* Personal branding components

### Prompts Become Requirements

The quality of the website depended heavily on the quality of the instructions provided.

Clear requirements produced better results.

### Personal Branding Matters

A portfolio website helps:

* Showcase projects
* Demonstrate skills
* Build credibility
* Create an online presence

## Biggest Insight

AI dramatically reduces the time required to go from idea to working website.

Instead of starting with a blank page, I started with a working foundation and improved from there.

